# App OS — buttons and transaction toast

One language for every commit control. Do not invent a second toast or spinner system.

## Ownership split

| Phase | Owner | UI |
|-------|--------|-----|
| Ready / intent | Button | `OsSheetAction` `ready` frame, or second-tap label (`Leave?`) |
| Working (wallet **and** chain wait) | Button | `PulsingDots` only — hide label |
| Success | Global toast | Green one-liner via `trackTransaction` or `setTxResult` |
| Fail | Global toast | Red one-liner |
| Social gesture | Control itself | Stand / endorse flip; toast **errors only** |

**No blue / pending toast in the app.** The toast is success or error only.

**Do not** use `succeeded` / green check morph on app action buttons. Success is always the toast.

## Handoff (required for NEAR txs)

```ts
setPending(true);           // button dots — wallet + chain wait
const response = await …;   // signAndSend / SDK write
const confirmed = await trackTransaction({
  txHashes,
  successMessage: txToastSuccess.…,
  failureMessage: txToastError.…,
});
// clear pending in finally (or after trackTransaction returns)
```

Keep the button `pending` through `trackTransaction`. Never clear dots before chain settle just to show a toast — there is no confirming toast.

`submittedMessage` / `txToastConfirming.*` are optional leftovers for call-site notes; they are **not** shown in the toast.

For off-chain / SDK `wait: true` sheet saves (profile, mood, page look):

```ts
// pending dots while save runs
on success: setTxResult({ type: 'success', msg: txToastSuccess.… }); close sheet
on error:   setTxResult({ type: 'error', msg: txToastError.… });
```

Do **not** also show an inline red error card for the same save failure — toast owns it. Inline alerts stay for session hints and field validation only.

Never mount a local `TransactionFeedbackToast` — root provider only.

## Rewards

- **Collect SOCIAL** — chip pulses through claim + chain wait; toast is green success only
- **Passive credits** — same glass toast (`+X SOCIAL · Stand`), not a custom burst pill
- Do not revive `AppRewardCreditBurst`

## Action taxonomy (one primitive)

Three orthogonal axes — do **not** invent a second Button tree or
`dangerPrimary` / `dangerGhost` style matrix.

| Axis | Values | Meaning |
|------|--------|---------|
| **Intent** | `primary` · `ghost` (secondary) · `danger` | What the action is |
| **State** | idle · `ready` · `pending` · disabled | Can they press / working |
| **Placement** | `sm` / `md` · borderless · stack / row | Where it lives |

`dismiss` may stay as a soft cousin of `ghost`; prefer `ghost` for new work.

### Placement recipes (app `src/lib`)

Same pill language — helpers only, never feature CSS:

| Helper | Intent | Use |
|--------|--------|-----|
| `OsEmptyAction` | primary `sm` | Empty / retry recoveries (Clear search, Try again, Browse Market) |
| `OsRowAction` | primary `sm` | List / header chips (Play, Collect, Read, See all) |
| `OsLoadMore` | ghost `sm` | Show more / Load more / Show less |
| `OsIconAction` | icon | Header / chrome icons (not a pill) |

Sheet footers use `OsSheetAction` directly (`md` stack). Market Buy / guild Join
use `OsSheetAction` `sm` in place.

### When to use which intent

- **primary** — one main commit per surface (Save, Buy, Collect, Join)
- **ghost** — Cancel, Show more, quiet secondary
- **danger** — Remove, Leave, Discard, Transfer — same chrome as primary, red intent, arms on `ready`

### Keep outside this pill system (different jobs)

- Stand / step back, endorse toggles — gesture flips; toast **errors only**
- Feed love / like / save / amplify — inline engagement
- Collect SOCIAL wallet chip — `os-surface-chip`
- Form choice chips (`os-surface-chip` / `os-choice-chip-row`)
- Guild structure discovery / reorder icon chips — compact custom until a chip recipe exists
- Accent Standing Discover (`StandingDiscoverLink`) — standing signal, not a generic CTA

## When to use `OsSheetAction`

**Use** for sheet/footer/form commit CTAs:

- Profile editor, storage deposit/withdraw/share
- Guild create, settings save, composer Post, add member/space
- Home feed composer Post
- Preview bars (mood / page look) — `layout="row-compact"` + `.os-commit-actions`
- Guild member role confirms (Move to mod, Remove, Transfer, …) — same commit chrome
- Proposal vote / confirm footers

**Do not** hand-roll `guild-secondary-button`, `market-sales-more`, `collection-reading-open`,
`launcher-home-retry`, `profile-support-retry`, or underlined retry links for the jobs
above — use the helpers. Clipboard / share success uses the global toast (see
`endorsementLinkCopied` / `recoveryCodeCopied`) — never `succeeded` morph on the pill.

## Commit chrome (Cancel + primary)

Shared classes: `.os-commit-actions` + `.os-commit-cancel`

- Text **Cancel** (muted) + compact primary chip — not a danger Cancel button
- Destructive secondary (Discard) may use `.os-commit-cancel.is-danger`
- Used by preview bars and notice-card confirms
- No mood tint on in-panel confirms; preview bars may whisper mood on the shell only

## Notice cards (info + confirm)

Shared component: `OsNoticeCard` (`@/components/ui/os-notice-card`)

One glass + type language for:

- **Info** (`align="center"` + `shell`) — How SOCIAL works → title, body, single primary (**Got it**)
- **Confirm** (`align="start"`, shell optional) — Discard, guild member role → title, optional meta/body, toggles, commit row
- Nested confirms (guild menu) use `shell={false}` inside the existing floating panel

Do not invent per-feature title/body/button CSS for these surfaces.

## Guild member confirms

- **Menu** for choosing an action; **OsNoticeCard** once chosen (same glass panel, not a menu list)
- Structure: title → who (meta) → consequence → optional toggles → commit row
- Do not repeat who in a read-only Member field
- Do not keep menu header chrome on the confirm step

## Preview bars (mood / page look)

- Copy: plain mood / look label (e.g. **Noir**) — no cryptic `Business · Noir` pairing required
- Layout: **one thin pill toolbar** above the dock — never a stacked confirmation card
- Actions: `.os-commit-actions` — text **Cancel** + compact primary **Save** chip (or `Unlock · N`); Save pulses while busy
- Shell: glass + soft top lip + whisper mood wash; toast owns success
- Do not show a second “saved” line on the bar

## Button API (app)

Prefer `OsSheetAction` / `OsSheetPrimaryAction`:

- `ready` — framed when dirty / commit-ready
- `pending` — dots only (`pendingLabel` is SR-only)
- **Do not pass `succeeded` / `succeededLabel` in app**

## Toast chrome

- One global status lane (bottom, above dock) — OS-column centered like preview bars
- Readable overlay fill (`bg/0.92`, blur 32, soft lip) — near dropdown opacity; **stable fill** (never retint on success/error)
- Soft chip radius (`~1.15rem`), not a capsule (capsule = controls)
- Color on the status icon + dismiss hairline (green/red); glass fill stays stable
- One-line body; **green/red icon only** — no pending/blue state
- Copy from `@/lib/transaction-toast-copy`

## “Confirm” in labels

Means **user intent** only (second tap, ready to commit). Never means chain confirmation — the button is still pulsing then.

## Sizing

`OsSheetAction` is full-width in stacks; `row-compact` for preview bars. Base min-height ~2.75rem; slightly taller from `sm`; slightly tighter under 380px. Do not invent per-screen button heights for sheet CTAs.
